# VELOCITY-3's three study scenarios, each simulated by Tomás Lindqvist on November 19, 2026 with the reference trial
# model (domain spec 3.4.4): the model's own output, as Run trial simulation wrote it. SSC-2 allows patients who failed a
# prior biologic, so the biostatistician assumed fewer screen failures (33 percent) and a lower response on treatment
# (43 percent). simulation.test.ts runs the model again and checks every figure here against it.

d:TS-1 a ls:TrialSimulation ;
  ls:identifier "TS-1" ;
  ls:trialSimulationRun lst:TrialSimulationRun-complete ;
  ls:simulates d:SSC-1 ;
  ls:scenarioAsOf "2026-11-19"^^xsd:date ;
  ls:simulatedTrials 2000 ;
  ls:recruitmentRate 0.5 ;
  ls:screenFailureRate 48.0 ;
  ls:dropoutRate 15.0 ;
  ls:controlResponse 35.0 ;
  ls:treatmentResponse 46.0 ;
  ls:saeRate 6.0 ;
  ls:assumedEffect "Response of 46 percent on treatment against 35 percent on control; 6 serious adverse events per 100 patient-years" ;
  ls:simulationModel "Reference trial model 1.0: a reference model, not validated for decisions about real studies" .

